1
00:00:05,261 --> 00:00:06,261
Hi everyone!

2
00:00:06,327 --> 00:00:08,960
Today, a tutorial on the "crossover".

3
00:00:09,834 --> 00:00:14,532
At first, it's not obvious
how your foot reaches the opposite pedal,

4
00:00:14,598 --> 00:00:16,181
it seems pretty far away.

5
00:00:16,247 --> 00:00:17,689
Actually, you can do it

6
00:00:17,713 --> 00:00:21,460
on any freestyle unicycle,
unless you have 140mm cranks.

7
00:00:22,601 --> 00:00:25,741
It's all about positioning:
turn your hips a bit,

8
00:00:25,774 --> 00:00:28,721
which makes it much easier
to do while turning.

9
00:00:29,234 --> 00:00:31,276
It'll probably rub a bit

10
00:00:31,300 --> 00:00:34,554
on the outside of your leg at first,
but that's completely normal.

11
00:00:34,557 --> 00:00:36,221
Over time, it'll rub less and less.

12
00:00:36,881 --> 00:00:40,460
The easiest way into the trick
is from a "wheel walk".

13
00:00:41,627 --> 00:00:45,295
The goal is to get
the opposite foot on the tire

14
00:00:45,361 --> 00:00:49,041
and the crank at the top,
so you can press down and start the trick.

15
00:00:49,654 --> 00:00:52,021
To get out, it's the reverse:

16
00:00:52,747 --> 00:00:54,588
bring your hips back in line.

17
00:00:55,007 --> 00:00:57,848
To get a feel for the position,
you can hold on to a wall,

18
00:00:57,914 --> 00:01:01,380
but that's not the best way,
since the trick turns naturally.

19
00:01:02,821 --> 00:01:05,996
I think the best way to learn
is to keep your foot on the wheel,

20
00:01:06,020 --> 00:01:09,767
as in a "glide",
so you get some momentum

21
00:01:09,833 --> 00:01:13,820
when you struggle
to bring the crank back up.

22
00:01:14,727 --> 00:01:19,681
Ride a circle as tight
or as wide as you like,

23
00:01:19,747 --> 00:01:22,114
and you can even go all the way
to a "spin" if you want.

24
00:01:23,014 --> 00:01:24,386
Once you're comfortable,

25
00:01:24,452 --> 00:01:25,854
if you're not sure
what to do with your foot,

26
00:01:25,878 --> 00:01:28,215
you can keep it close to the other one,

27
00:01:28,301 --> 00:01:31,220
it looks a bit nicer.

28
00:01:32,667 --> 00:01:35,341
The first variation
is the "crossover toe point spin",

29
00:01:35,407 --> 00:01:37,941
which you can also use as a mount.

30
00:01:38,574 --> 00:01:42,295
Next, there's what I call the "snake",

31
00:01:42,361 --> 00:01:45,340
where you wedge your foot
behind the frame.

32
00:01:45,406 --> 00:01:52,245
[Music]

